{"hw":"δήπου","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">δήπου</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">δήπου</span>, indef. <span class=\"lex-gram\">Adv.</span> (better written <span class=\"lex-orth gk\">δή που</span>) <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">perhaps, it may be,</b> <span class=\"gk\">ᾧ δή που ἀδελφεὸν ἔκτανε</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">24.736</span> </span>: in Trag. and <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Att.</span> </span> usu. <b class=\"lex-tr\">doubtless, I presume,</b> <span class=\"gk\">οὐ δήπου τλητόν</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1064</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τῶν Ααΐου δ. τις ὠνομάζετο</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">OT</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1042</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Ar.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pl.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">491</span> </span>,<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">582</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Th.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.121</span> </span>, etc.; <span class=\"gk\">ἴστε γὰρ δή που, μέμνησθε γὰρ δή που,</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">D.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.25</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">19.113</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">18.249</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">σχεδὸν ἴσμεν ἅπαντες δή που</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">3.9</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">οὐδεὶς ἀγνοεῖ δή που</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">21.156</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">II</span> asinterrog. implying an affirm. answer, <span class=\"gk\">τὴν αἰχμάλωτον κάτοισθα δή που;</span> i.e. <b class=\"lex-tr\">I presume</b> you know, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Tr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">418</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ἀνόμοιον δή που</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Tht.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">159b</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">οὐ δή που;</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">surely it is</b> not <b class=\"lex-tr\">so?</b> implying a neg. answer, as <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Ar.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ra.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">526</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Men.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">73c</span> </span>.</div></div>"}